# Official spec-kit install-time copy exclusion (gitignore syntax): everything
# listed here is development-only material that `specify extension add` must
# NEVER copy into a consuming repository's `.specify/extensions/jira/`.
# (This file itself is always excluded automatically.)
tests/
specs/
.specify/
.github/
.claude/
.tokensave/
.editorconfig
.gitignore
.shellcheckrc
PSScriptAnalyzerSettings.psd1
coverage.xml
testResults.xml
# The coverage runner's output directory. It is gitignored, so it exists only on
# a machine that has measured coverage — but `specify extension add --dev` copies
# the working tree, not the git index, and this directory holds a NAMED PIPE
# (the xtrace fifo). Python's copytree refuses to copy one, so the install fails
# outright on any developer machine where the gate has been run.
coverage/

# Golden "before" captures a feature's own test plan records at repo root
# (e.g. specs/029, T001-T003), gitignored for the same reason as coverage/:
# they exist only on a machine that has run the capture, and a --dev install
# would otherwise copy that machine-specific snapshot into the consumer tree.
.baseline/

# Architecture and vision documentation. It describes how the extension is BUILT
# — the engine/sink boundary, the twin ports, the Windows probe loop, the
# roadmap — none of which a consuming repository needs to run the bridge; README
# and INSTALL are the consumer-facing pair. Nothing in the installed surface
# links here, and these documents cite `.specify/memory/constitution.md`, which
# is itself development-only, so shipping them would plant broken links.
docs/

# Contributor instructions for developing THIS extension. A coding agent working
# in a consuming repository discovers nested instruction files and would read
# them as its own marching orders — being told to keep a Windows conformance
# corpus green and to run `tests/run-bash.sh`, neither of which is installed.
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md

# `* text=auto eol=lf` is unanchored, so wherever this file lands it governs its
# whole subtree. Installed, it would impose this repository's LF policy on the
# consumer's tree — a policy that exists to protect OUR Windows test fixtures
# and is none of their business.
.gitattributes

# The `--dev` copy route walks the working tree, not the git index, so without
# this entry it copies this repository's own .git directory — 6 165 files,
# 38 MB of history — into every consuming repository (research R5, FR-002a).
# The zip route is unaffected: `git ls-files` never lists `.git/`.
.git/

# The release-artifact builder and its gates (packaging/build-artifact.sh,
# packaging/verify-artifact.sh, packaging/publish-artifact.sh). Development
# tooling a consuming repository cannot use and must not receive
# (Principle XV, research R10).
packaging/
